A||N||9||87GTBro||Exhaust pipe replacement cost???||||5||
Z||000000||87GTBro||01-01-2000||04:08 AM||||Does anyone know the average price for replacing the exhaust pipe from the cat to the muffler on a V6 GT?||||reg||5
Z||000001||JetroGT||01-02-2000||03:34 AM||||I actually had my exhaust replaced from the down pipe back, including new tips. It was about $600. Just subtract the cost of a cat. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||cobra427||01-02-2000||03:53 AM||||A good s/s Bola system from cat forward will run you around $550.00. Nice setup!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||01-02-2000||12:49 PM||||I don't think you guys read his post... Replacing the pipe you're talking about shouldn't cost more than 50 bucks installed. It shouldn't be difficult at all.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||01-02-2000||01:57 PM||||On a similar note...Where can I get a Borla system? I am in the market for a new system. I notice that when my car is cold and I drive it, I can here that dreaded tick, tick, tick sound. But once it is warm, all is well. It also happens from a hard start as well.  ||||reg||2
Z||000005||Bruce||01-02-2000||02:16 PM||||Wis. GT,<BR>Contact George at the Fiero Shop. He's selling a custom Fiero-made Borla system. He's on the web at www/fieroshop.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroshop||01-02-2000||02:20 PM||||GT Bastard is right. The one section of ppipe should only cost between $50.00 and $75.00 installed. It will cost more if it is made of stainless||||reg||12
Z||000007||cobra427||01-02-2000||06:38 PM||||WisGT, here is another place to find the Bola exhaust,  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/notes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/notes.html</A>      Look at Tim Perrigo and click on Parts and Appraisels there you will find your Bola exhaust. cheers||||reg||1
Z||000008||Boxdin||01-04-2000||02:47 PM||||When we replaced the muffler sys on my 88 Formula, we were amazed to find out that we could buy a new muffler  ( with the "head pipe" and outlet pipes ) for only 135.00. And it was a walker part. The only other parts are the two headers, crossover, and tips. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||01-04-2000||03:30 PM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carparts.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.wrenchead.com" TARGET=_blank>www.wrenchead.com</A>  to check prices for the pipe you're looking for.<P>If you're the do-it yourself type, these folks are cheaper than just about everyone on the planet.||||reg||1
